(load "carp-diagnostics.carp")

(Project.config "title" "carp-diagnostics")
(Project.config "docs-directory" "./docs/")
(Project.config "docs-logo" "")
(Project.config "docs-url" "https://github.com/carpentry-org/carp-diagnostics")
(Project.config "docs-styling" "../style.css")
(Project.config "docs-prelude" "Structured logging and hierarchical profiling
for Carp.

```
(load \"git@github.com:carpentry-org/carp-diagnostics@master\")
```

- [`Diagnostics`](./Diagnostics.html) — logging, error state, and zone profiling
- [`LogLevel`](./LogLevel.html) — `Debug` through `Critical`
- [`ZoneStats`](./ZoneStats.html) — accumulated timings for one zone
- [`ActiveTimer`](./ActiveTimer.html) — an open zone

Zones nest and are usually opened with `with-zone`, which cannot leak an open
timer the way a mismatched `start-zone!`/`end-zone!` pair can:

```
(let-do [d (Diagnostics.new \"game.log\")]
  (Diagnostics.with-zone &d \"Total Frame Time\"
    (Diagnostics.with-zone &d \"Physics\" (step-physics))
    (Diagnostics.with-zone &d \"Render\" (draw)))
  (Diagnostics.print-stats! &d))
```

`print-stats!` reports count, average, min, max and standard deviation per
zone. Name a zone `\"Total Frame Time\"` and every other zone is also reported
as a percentage of it, which is the number that says where the frame went.
Stats are kept as a running sum and sum of squares, so nothing grows with the
number of samples.")

(save-docs Diagnostics LogLevel ZoneStats ActiveTimer)
; Carp's save-docs hardcodes the index filename as <title>_index.html.
; Rename to docs/index.html.
(defn main []
  (System.system "mv ./docs/carp-diagnostics_index.html ./docs/index.html"))
